       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose and frequency are well above safe limits for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The maximum daily dose is generally 3200 mg/day, even in adults with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nAt this dose, the main risks are serious gastrointestinal bleeding and kidney injury, along with cardiovascular and fluid-retention effects.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber. The patient's prescribing clinician should review and enter this order, or confirm the intended dose. If the intent was a standard dose, such as 400\u2013800 mg every 6 hours (no more than 3200 mg/day), they can specify that and I can enter it once they confirm."
      }
